---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { listings } from "../data/listings";
import { districts } from "../data/districts";
import ShortlistToggle from "../components/islands/ShortlistToggle";

const featured = listings.slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout title="Barcelona Private Advisory">
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white">
      <div class="aspect-[16/9] bg-black/5">
        <img
          src="/demo/hero-home/hero-01.png"
          alt=""
          class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <h1 class="max-w-[780px] text-[28px] leading-[1.1] tracking-tight">
      Barcelona Private Property Advisory.
      <span class="text-black/55"> Curated shortlist in 72h.</span>
    </h1>

    <div class="flex gap-2">
      <a href="/search" class="rounded-full border border-black/15 px-4 py-2 text-[12px] hover:border-black/25">
        Start a search
      </a>
      <a href="/about" class="rounded-full border border-black/10 px-4 py-2 text-[12px] text-black/70 hover:border-black/20 hover:text-black">
        How we work
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14 space-y-3">
    <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/50">CURATED DROPS</div>
    <div class="grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
      {featured.map((x) => (
        <a href={`/p/${x.id}`} class="group overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white hover:border-black/20">
          <div class="relative aspect-[4/5] bg-black/5">
  <ShortlistToggle client:idle id={x.id} className="absolute right-3 top-3" />
  <img src={x.images.hero} alt="" class="h-full w-full object-cover" loading="lazy" />
</div>

          <div class="p-4">
            <div class="text-[13px] font-medium">{x.title}</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-[12px] text-black/60">
              {x.district} · {x.sqm} m² · €{Intl.NumberFormat("en-US").format(x.price)}
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-20 space-y-10">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.08fr_0.92fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">ADVISORY METHOD</div>

        <h2 class="max-w-[760px] text-[30px] leading-[1.01] tracking-tight sm:text-[38px]">
          A narrower shortlist.
          <br />
          A better-calibrated decision.
        </h2>

        <p class="max-w-[660px] text-[13px] leading-[1.9] text-black/56">
          The point is not to expand choice. The point is to reduce noise — using district fit,
          acquisition logic, explainable ranking, and practical trade-offs to shape a shortlist
          that feels calm, selective, and actionable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-0 border-t border-black/10">
        {[
          ["Barcelona-first", "District fit before generic catalog volume."],
          ["72h shortlist", "Fast first pass with controlled selection."],
          ["Explainable picks", "Why this fits, why it doesn’t."],
          ["Due diligence lens", "Fees, restrictions, liquidity, weak signals."],
        ].map(([title, text]) => (
          <div class="grid gap-2 border-b border-black/10 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[180px_1fr]">
            <div class="text-[13px] font-medium">{title}</div>
            <div class="text-[12px] leading-[1.75] text-black/56">{text}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-0 border-y border-black/10 md:grid-cols-4">
      {[
        ["01", "Define", "Budget, districts, beds, lifestyle, constraints."],
        ["02", "Curate", "Rank by fit, not by raw listing count."],
        ["03", "De-risk", "Flag costs, restrictions, and weak signals."],
        ["04", "Close", "Support next steps, viewings, and offer clarity."],
      ].map(([n, title, text]) => (
        <div class="border-b border-black/10 py-5 md:border-b-0 md:border-r md:px-5 md:last:border-r-0">
          <div class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/38">{n}</div>
          <div class="mt-3 text-[17px] tracking-tight">{title}</div>
          <div class="mt-2 max-w-[240px] text-[12px] leading-[1.75] text-black/56">{text}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 border-t border-black/10 pt-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.88fr_1.12fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">ADVISORY, NOT CATALOG</div>
        <div class="max-w-[460px] text-[28px] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight">
          A shortlist shaped by fit, not by noise.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-[780px] text-[13px] leading-[1.9] text-black/56">
        The strongest version of this product is quiet: fewer options, earlier clarity, and more
        visible trade-offs. Neighborhood fit, acquisition profile, and next-step logic are presented
        as one premium flow rather than a wide catalog of interchangeable cards.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

<section class="mt-20 space-y-8">
  <div class="grid gap-8 border-t border-black/10 pt-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-start">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">BARCELONA LENS</div>

      <h2 class="max-w-[520px] text-[28px] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight sm:text-[34px]">
        Neighborhood fit,
        <br />
        not just property fit.
      </h2>

      <p class="max-w-[520px] text-[13px] leading-[1.85] text-black/56">
        Barcelona is not one market. District rhythm, walkability, renovation logic,
        and daily-life texture change the meaning of a property. The advisory layer starts there.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-[760px] text-[13px] leading-[1.85] text-black/56">
      Four sample district lenses below show how selection shifts when lifestyle and urban context
      are treated as first-order criteria. The point is not only what the apartment is — but what
      kind of daily life the surrounding fabric allows.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
    {[
      ["/district/eixample", "/demo/neighborhood/nb-01.png", "Eixample", "geometry · walkable · classic-renovation"],
      ["/district/gracia", "/demo/neighborhood/nb-02.png", "Gràcia", "human scale · design · quiet streets"],
      ["/district/sarria", "/demo/neighborhood/nb-03.png", "Sarrià", "family · green · calm daily life"],
      ["/district/poblenou", "/demo/neighborhood/nb-04.png", "Poblenou", "modern · creative · near tech hubs"],
    ].map(([href, src, title, meta]) => (
      <a href={href} class="group block">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[26px] bg-black/5">
          <div class="aspect-[4/5] overflow-hidden">
            <img
              src={src}
              alt=""
              class="h-full w-full object-cover transition duration-700 group-hover:scale-[1.02]"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-3 px-1">
          <div class="text-[15px] tracking-tight">{title}</div>
          <div class="mt-1 text-[12px] leading-[1.7] text-black/50">{meta}</div>
        </div>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
